{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789508433,"nonce":"ToY5uY9dOshJX5+DJiSCWBqWNrg=","title":"review-tui: followup reply preview shows untrimmed body","message":"FollowupReplyPreviewScreen renders the reply buffer exactly as the editor\nleft it, but the review TUI send path trims it first, so the preview does\nnot show what actually gets mailed.\n\n_modals.py:583 (FollowupReplyPreviewScreen.on_mount) does:\n\n    body = b4.append_email_signature(self._reply_text)\n\nwhile _review_app.py:1909 (_send_followup_reply) does:\n\n    reply_text = b4.review._trim_quoted_reply(text)\n    reply_text_with_sig = b4.append_email_signature(reply_text)\n\n_trim_quoted_reply() strips the leading \"#\" instruction header, drops\n\"| \" external-reviewer lines, resolves standalone \"\u003e--cut--\" markers, and\ndrops the trailing run of quoted/blank lines below the last comment. None\nof that is reflected in the preview, so the preview shows b4's own \"#\"\nscaffolding and the raw \"\u003e--cut--\" marker as if they were about to be\nmailed, plus quoted context that will in fact be trimmed away.\n\nThe marker case is the most confusing one: the instruction header tells\nthe user that b4 resolves \"\u003e--cut--\" when they send, but the preview they\nare asked to confirm still shows the unresolved marker and the context it\nis going to discard.\n\nThe fix is presumably to trim in on_mount() the same way the send path\ndoes, rather than to stop trimming on send.\n\nSecond, related inconsistency: the lite view's send path\n(_lite_app.py:800, _send_reply) does not call _trim_quoted_reply() at all.\nIts preview is therefore honest, but a trailing quoted run that the review\npanel would trim is sent verbatim from the lite view. The lite composer\ndoes not emit the \"#\" instruction header, so no b4 scaffolding leaks into\nthe sent mail there.\n\nBoth predate the signature series merged in 165704a; that merge only moved\nthe duplicated signature-append code into b4.append_email_signature() and\ndid not change the trimming behaviour on either path.","files":null}]}